WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.420
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.460
Into the VRAINS!

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.930
Stop hiding and come out!

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:22.640
Will that card open the door to my heart?

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.690
Blue Angel will descend into your heart!

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.620
And save your soul!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.980
Take Blue Angel's blue love!

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.160
Huh?

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:40.590
When the door to my heart opened, 
there was still one card left.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:49.070
Goodbye, Aoi Zaizen.  The pathetic 
girl who couldn't become a blue angel.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:55.420
I now break Blue Angel's wings 
to take everything from her!

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.540
Aoi!

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:02.610
You're...

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.300
Dr. Kogami!

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.110
Aren't you dead?

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.700
I did die.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.710
But I resurrected.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.690
Move out of the way!

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.620
I can't let you pass.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:20.690
You'll meet the same fate as Blue Angel.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.800
Oh well.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.700
I'll have to use my trump card.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:29.940
Zaizen?

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.500
You play very dirty!

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.680
Do you know how many people 
you dragged into this?

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.920
It all started because you hid the Ignis.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.160
This is the finale!

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:49.290
I was waiting for this.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.190
My sacred mother tree!

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:57.400
Playmaker, your defeat is assured.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.870
Have conviction, Playmaker!

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.110
Don't lose track of the big picture!

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:07.070
I can't believe I lost.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.880
But I don't regret a thing.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.410
Playmaker, how about you?

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.380
I told you.  I'll no longer have doubt.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.250
I can't let you go any further.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.820
Are you Revolver?

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.160
You're Go Onizuka.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.130
Sink into the abyss of bottomless despair!

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.500
So you destroyed them all.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.770
We always duel alone.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:43.020
That's why I decided to fight for myself!

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:47.510
For my thirst for victory 
that's deep in my heart!

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:52.250
Fine.  As you wish.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.320
Electric Borrelsword Slash!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.500
Go Onizuka has 0 LP.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.840
Playmaker!  This was the best I could do.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.080
I leave the rest to you.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.520
Playmaker.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.250
It's finally time to bring this to an end.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.260
Yeah.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:48.720
I run Across the universe

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.890
At the speed of light

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.760
Begin Loading

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:57.490
Open the door of dreams

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:01.060
VRAINS spreads

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.170
Believe in myself

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.700
VRAINS continues

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:13.010
The circuit draws the future

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:17.080
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:18.680
Access!

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.380
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:22.980
I'm now With the Wind

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.290
Link with my soul

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.060
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.790
Now Win the Race

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.630
Connected world

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:36.130
No matter when

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.500
Nothing is impossible

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:43.640
Strive for hope

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:48.210
And ride the wind!

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.470
Revolver, I won't let you 
have your way anymore!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:19.610
Then let's settle this in a duel.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.730
Follow me, Playmaker!

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.670
My tail's gone!

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.410
Boss, are you okay?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:09.410
Compared to the regret of failing to broadcast 
Go Onizuka's duel to the end,

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.220
this pain is nothing!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.850
Umm, it's already healed.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.020
Really?  That's good.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.730
I was worried I'd have 
to pay a lot to fix it.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.170
Boss!  Look at that!

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:26.700
What is it?

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.320
That's Playmaker and Revolver!

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:34.750
They're going to Speed Duel there?

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.170
That's crazy!

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.770
Why aren't they broadcasting?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.050
Are there complications?

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.250
That's Yusaku and Revolver.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.740
Ten years after the incident, 
will this be the final duel?

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:59.870
Since Dr. Kogami is dead, only Revolver 
knows the truth about what happened ten years ago.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.680
To let my brother know what happened...

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.040
...defeat Revolver and 
learn the truth, Yusaku!

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.790
You're really gonna duel here?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.150
Having many lives won't be enough.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:25.250
You said that you only have one goal.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.490
To kill the Ignis.

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:34.100
So you're destroying the network 
and plunging the world into chaos.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:38.340
Do you need to do this 
just to kill the Ignis?

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:43.680
This wouldn't have happened if 
you simply gave me that Ignis.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.650
I have no intention of stopping this plan.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:51.750
Ignis!  I will kill you!

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:01.430
Boss!  It's too dangerous to get any closer!

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:05.260
We can't hear them, but let's film from here!

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.630
No audio is fine!

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:12.100
Just make sure to get the video!

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.250
Okay!

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:17.020
We must broadcast this duel to everyone!

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:22.130
This'll be a historical duel that 
people will talk about forever!

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:26.680
It's your fault that many duelists fell.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.960
I promise to defeat you with my own hands!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.960
Go ahead and try.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.660
You'll also become a victim!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.510
Speed Duel!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.290
I'll go first!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.200
You'll get the ball rolling?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.780
You're so motivated, Playmaker!

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.480
I summon Stack Reviver!

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:04.260
When a Cyberse-Type is summoned, I can 
Special Summon Boot Staggered from my hand!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:13.770
And when a Cyberse-Type is on the field, 
I can Special Summon Backup Secretary!

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:20.250
All right!  Let's do this!

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:23.580
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.280
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:29.650
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:35.650
I set Backup Secretary, Stack Reviver 
and Boot Staggered in the Link Markers!

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:40.970
Link Summon!

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:44.900
Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:55.380
Yeah!  You arleady brought out Decode Talker!

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:00.910
When Stack Reviver is used to Link Summon...

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:06.820
...I can resurrect a different Level 4 or 
lower Cyberse that was used to Link Summon.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.750
I Special Summon Backup 
Secretary in defense position!

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:18.900
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for 
every monster next to its link.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:20.900
Power Integration!

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.280
Playmaker!  Above!

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:38.580
They're able to duel while 
avoiding the debris!

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.190
But you're not!

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.760
Unlike you, Playmaker has good reflexes.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:55.790
When our minds are one, Revolver 
is no match for us!  Right?

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.970
I set one card and end my turn.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.950
This is going well!

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.650
Beat up Revolver!

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:09.420
What an arrogant AI.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:17.600
Playmaker, do you know why that 
Ignis is running from the Hanoi?

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:20.700
So I can live, of course!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:26.400
By the time I captured it, it 
already lost most of its memories.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:30.010
So it said it didn't remember anything?

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:36.860
Ignis is programmed by Dr. 
Kogami's special algorithm.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:42.190
It seems you couldn't decipher it, 
so you believed what that Ignis said.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:43.980
However...

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:56.430
In the data we retrieved from that Ignis, 
nothing was related to its memories.

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:01.030
That means they're still inside that Ignis.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:08.410
That Ignis's Control ID is IGN006.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:12.740
An artificial intelligence linked 
to the sixth test subject.

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:18.310
In other words, that AI was 
modeled after you, Playmaker.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:19.240
What?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:26.060
While the six kidnapped children 
were forced to duel in VR...

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:33.530
...behind the scenes, those duels were 
used to create six AI with free will.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:39.470
That was the true goal of the Lost Incident.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:44.910
That Ignis was created by 
observing and analyzing you.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:53.190
And the Ignis were supposed to save humanity.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:57.860
But the Ignis grew quicker 
than humans could imagine.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:01.790
They created the Cyberse World, 
the world of the Ignis.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.760
Cyberse World?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:11.370
That Ignis hid the Cyberse World somewhere 
in the network in order to protect its kin.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:16.680
What's important is that instead 
of telling you the truth...

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:21.880
...that Ignis pretended to lose its 
memories and kept misleading you.

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:26.910
If an AI evolves to the 
point that it can lie...

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:30.340
...that's a terrifying threat to humanity.

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:35.320
That's why the Hanoi are trying 
to eradicate the Ignis.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:40.200
Are you still going to 
trust that AI, Playmaker?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.470
Umm...  Don't get the wrong idea!

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.940
Listen to me, Playmaker!

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:50.410
Umm...  Back then, I...

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:58.490
Found you, Ignis!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:02.920
Where's an escape route?  Where?

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.230
Come to me!

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.400
Welcome.  You're going to be our savior.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.620
Huh?  What?

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:24.180
Of course I realized that 
you were the same kid.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:29.580
But I was focused on escaping 
and didn't trust anyone.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:33.990
So I didn't know if I could trust you either.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.850
You're going to keep lying?

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:43.800
There's nothing between me and him.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.990
What'll happen to our strong friendship?

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.740
I never thought of you as a friend.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.710
I never felt friendship with you.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.950
Then why are you keeping me?

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.980
You're just a hostage.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.380
Oh yeah.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:09.110
I don't care about this AI.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.610
This battle is between you and me.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:14.200
Let's continue the duel!

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:21.850
Fine.  I'll defeat you 
and destroy that Ignis!

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.320
I don't care about this AI.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:37.320
This battle is between you and me.

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.920
Let's continue the duel!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:47.020
Fine.  I'll defeat you 
and destroy that Ignis!

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:50.420
Up ahead!

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.070
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:03.550
Destiny says to crush you without mercy.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:08.100
I summon Spin-Headed Behemoth!

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:14.050
I set one card and end my turn.

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:23.160
We have Decode Talker with 2800 ATK, but he 
put a monster with 800 ATK in attack position.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.500
And that set card...

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.400
This is clearly suspicious.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.940
Be quiet!

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.600
Sorry.

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:37.740
Umm...  Above you!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.140
Be careful, Yusaku!

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:49.620
Even a tiny fragment will kill you 
if it strikes you in the wrong place!

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.720
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:56.060
I summon Foal Tolelancer!

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:06.240
Foal Tolelancer's effect activates!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.710
It switches itself to defense position!

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:14.530
Foal Tolelancer in defense position?

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.580
Be careful of Revolver.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:29.170
He has a terrifying card-

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.570
What?

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:39.200
Ghost Girl and Go Onizuka...

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:44.220
Thanks to their sacrifices, I learned 
that Revolver has Mirror Force.

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:49.380
As long as Foal Tolelancer 
is in defense position...

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:53.050
...effects can't destroy my 
monsters in attack position!

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:57.800
That means Decode Talker won't be destroyed!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.030
Let's battle!

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.040
Go, Decode Talker!

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.430
I see.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.930
Attack Spin-Headed Behemoth!

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:10.240
Decode End!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:12.740
As you wish, I'll show it to you!

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:16.640
Kneel before Hanoi's noble power!

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:21.680
I activate the trap card, Mirror Force!

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.000
What?

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:29.720
This light...  Can't be...

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.070
I knew it!  Mirror Force!

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:33.060
But...

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.470
Why activate it when he knows it won't work?

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:40.200
Spin-Headed Behemoth's effect activates!

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:43.130
When this monster is attacked,

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:47.390
all your monsters in defense 
position switch to attack position!

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:55.550
You thought that was enough to stop it?

00:18:55.550 --> 00:19:01.450
Due to Mirror Force's effect, all your 
monsters in attack position are destroyed!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.770
What destructive power!

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:15.330
When an effect destroys 
a monster on the field,

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:18.740
I Special Summon Overflow 
Dragon from my hand.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:26.620
And when at least two cards are destroyed...

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:32.680
...Overflow Dragon's effect Special 
Summons an Overflow Token.

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:36.560
I can't stay quiet!

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:40.000
I don't care if you trust me or not!

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.880
If you lose, I'm dead too!

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.680
I end my turn.

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:49.370
Revolver has three monsters on his field.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:52.340
His next monster will be at least Link 3!

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.040
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:01.510
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:03.980
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:07.950
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Dragons!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:15.530
I set Overflow Dragon, Overflow Token and 
Spin-Headed Behemoth in the Link Markers!

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:23.080
Link Summon!

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:27.870
Appear, Link 3 Flash Charge Dragon!

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:36.310
Another dangerous-looking dragon!

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:42.260
Then from my hand, I summon Blast 
Powder Dragon and activate its effect!

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:49.430
Flash Charge Dragon gains 800 
ATK until the end of the turn!

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:53.740
Flash Charge Dragon attacks you directly!

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:03.810
Dirty Rush Supremacy!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.400
Playmaker!  Are you okay?

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.790
Yusaku!

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:20.820
Blast Powder Dragon has 800 ATK.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:25.200
Even if you take a direct attack, 
you'll still have 100 LP left.

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:28.500
Don't underestimate me.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:30.500
Blast Powder Dragon's effect!

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:39.260
When a monster powered up by this card 
deals battle damage, it gains 800 ATK.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:43.700
What?  If we take this 
attack, we're out of LP!

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:45.720
This is bad!

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:49.790
This is the end, Playmaker!

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:52.970
Blast Powder Dragon attacks you directly!

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.690
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:22.830
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:30.030
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:37.410
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:44.630
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:48.790
There were fragments of power

00:22:49.020 --> 00:22:55.960
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:03.300
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.430 --> 00:23:10.510
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:17.710
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:24.590
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:32.260
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:36.490 --> 00:23:44.280
